## Findings that change the plan

**F1 (P1, blocker) — the port is not in this branch.** Item 3's premise is false here: `clojure.cljc:1136` still rejects with *"Portable try requires one Exception/ExceptionInfo catch and no finally"*, `src/cljc/yang/clojure/` has zero hits for `%capture`/`clj.rt/ctx`/`provenance`, and `cell/dsg__new-provenance` exists only in the python and php preludes. The new legs therefore fail at **compile** time, not runtime — the dispatch's pre-authorised §8.10.8 diagnosis does not apply. Kit and port (`exception-r3-impl` @ `854b74c3`) must be composed before shiva measures anything. I did not merge/rebase: that touches `src/` and is an orchestrator decision.

**F2 (P1) — the two-file list was incomplete.** `exception_legs.clj:106-111` held an active generate-time `throw`. Removing only the matrix exclusion would not have reddened three legs: that `throw` sits inside `run-pair`'s `try`, so it would have errored *every* leg of *every* clojure-caller pair, and `all-directed-pair-sources-compile-test` (no `try`) would have failed outright. The ruling names this file as one of "the three kit locations", so I treated the list as an omission.

**F3 (P2) — I did not pin "result 2".** In Clojure, `(try 1 (finally 2))` ⇒ **1**; `finally`'s value is discarded. Pinning 2 would encode the dialect divergence the owner's principle forbids. The DECIDED section names no value, so I pinned compilation and left runtime to the pair leg.

**F4 (P2) — the new legs' direction is inverted in the brief.** The predicate filters `caller = :clojure` and the arrow is donor→caller, so the live rows are `python→clojure`, `php→clojure`, `typescript→clojure`. **F5:** `-v` targeting is impossible — `yang.call.exception-contract` has zero `deftest`s, hence the new single-leg pin. **F6:** only `python-to-clojure-test` exists, so two of the three new rows are compiled but **never executed**.

